message.content:
The main issues are:

1. **Wrong comparison target**:  
   ```rust
   if data[i] == max_val
   ```
   This compares the current element to the **best value so far**, not to the value of the **current streak**. That can both break streaks incorrectly and accidentally merge non-consecutive equal values.

2. **The final streak is never checked**:  
   After the loop ends, the code never compares the last run to `max_count`, so a longest streak at the end of the vector can be missed.

Here is the corrected function:

<solution language="rust" verdict="fix">
fn longest_streak(data: &Vec<i32>) -> (i32, usize) {
    let mut max_val = data[0];
    let mut max_count: usize = 1;
    let mut current_val = data[0];
    let mut current_count: usize = 1;

    for i in 1..data.len() {
        if data[i] == current_val {
            current_count += 1;
        } else {
            if current_count > max_count {
                max_count = current_count;
                max_val = current_val;
            }

            current_val = data[i];
            current_count = 1;
        }
    }

    if current_count > max_count {
        max_count = current_count;
        max_val = current_val;
    }

    (max_val, max_count)
}
</solution>

